      "content": "To dismantle the meritocracy argument, first *acknowledge* the ideal of merit, then *redefine* \"merit\" to include the necessary starting resources. Argue that \"merit\" is only truly possible when access to quality education, healthcare, and stable capital is equitable from the beginning. You can then assert that systemic bias (like redlining or biased hiring in high-wealth sectors) actively distorts the \"merit\" system, making the outcome less about individual effort and more about inherited advantage. This reframing shows that the system is rigged *against* pure merit, making the intervention necessary.",
